+    The solver reconstructs every unique rectangle pair under rotations/flips.
+    To avoid hidden color-id semantics, the even checkerboard cells use the
+    color of the fragment that owns the reconstructed rectangle's top-left cell.
+    The generator always chooses that fragment to be the lower-numbered color,
+    so the visible behavior matches the prompt while staying ARC-like.
+    """
